    narr:narration """This narrative defines the product by opposition and early commercial framing: [real-time chat named as the anti-pattern](narr:Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat), against which the category is [deliberately created as a structured async decision platform](narr:Position_ProductCategoryAsyncPlatform). The initial [ICP](narr:Position_TargetMarketRemoteTeams) is [remote teams of 10-50 people](narr:Position_TargetMarketRemoteTeams), sized to feel decision-loss pain. Commercial framing starts at [a $12/user/month price point](narr:Position_PricingTwelveDollars), which a later sprint retro records moving upward for larger teams.""" ;
